# UI Style Consistency

- Follow the existing visual language of this project for all UI work.
- Do not introduce new visual patterns when an equivalent project pattern already exists.
- Reuse existing primitives, spacing rhythm, border radius, typography scale, and color tokens (`bg-surface`, `border-border`, muted text styles, existing button variants).
- New blocks/components must look native to current screens, not like a separate design system.
- Prefer extending existing components over creating one-off styled elements.
- Keep interaction patterns consistent with the current app (hover/active states, chips, cards, pills, badges, form controls).

## Before finishing UI changes

- Compare new UI with neighboring screens/components and align mismatches.
- If a style choice is unclear, default to the closest existing pattern in the same feature area.
